@slow
Feature: HTTP hardening requirements for the application (acceptance criteria)
  Written as requirements. A failing scenario is a finding that must be fixed or formally accepted
  in security/accepted-risks.json.

  Background:
    Given "curl" is installed
    And the following profile:
      | name     | value                 |
      | hostname | http://127.0.0.1:3000 |

  Scenario: Content-Type sniffing is disabled
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -sI <hostname>/
      """
    Then the output should contain:
      """
      X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
      """

  Scenario: Clickjacking protection header is set
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -sI <hostname>/
      """
    Then the output should contain:
      """
      X-Frame-Options
      """

  Scenario: A Content-Security-Policy header is set
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -sI <hostname>/
      """
    Then the output should contain:
      """
      Content-Security-Policy
      """

  Scenario: The framework version is not disclosed
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -sI <hostname>/
      """
    Then the output should not contain:
      """
      X-Powered-By
      """

  Scenario: The FTP directory listing is not public
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s <hostname>/ftp
      """
    Then the output should not contain:
      """
      acquisitions.md
      """

  Scenario: The metrics endpoint is not public
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w "status=%{http_code}" <hostname>/metrics
      """
    Then the output should not contain:
      """
      status=200
      """
